  "question": {
    "text": "The distances of the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>)</mo></math> from the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math> measured along a straight line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>k</mi></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> is"
  },
